1
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:36,320
[Kill Lu Ye]

2
00:00:39,930 --> 00:00:41,260
What are you doing here?

3
00:00:41,810 --> 00:00:42,770
Same as you.

4
00:00:43,610 --> 00:00:45,650
Smith doesn't trust your Shisha Gang.

5
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:47,450
So he sent the Qingtian Gang too.

6
00:00:47,570 --> 00:00:48,170
Let's go.

7
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:50,580
Young Master Lu.

8
00:00:50,850 --> 00:00:52,050
Are we close?

9
00:00:52,990 --> 00:00:53,930
Are we not?

10
00:00:54,290 --> 00:00:55,950
I thought we were quite close.

11
00:00:57,130 --> 00:00:58,060
After you, then.

12
00:01:08,190 --> 00:01:10,700
[Eclipse in the Lost City] [Episode 10]

13
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:19,200
Guess why Smith sent me here.

14
00:01:24,370 --> 00:01:25,770
It's nothing, really.

15
00:01:26,170 --> 00:01:27,690
I just told him some

16
00:01:27,810 --> 00:01:30,010
little stories about your Shisha Gang.

17
00:01:30,289 --> 00:01:31,330
For example,

18
00:01:32,330 --> 00:01:33,530
a sheriff defected

19
00:01:33,930 --> 00:01:35,930
and became the second-in-command,

20
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:37,250
making others unhappy

21
00:01:37,330 --> 00:01:39,190
and causing trouble everywhere.

22
00:01:39,729 --> 00:01:40,890
Or, for example,

23
00:01:41,770 --> 00:01:44,170
this former sheriff had also been injured,

24
00:01:44,210 --> 00:01:46,009
with two of his ribs just broken.

25
00:01:49,970 --> 00:01:52,500
Smith thought the Shisha Gang
is unreliable,

26
00:01:53,250 --> 00:01:54,170
so he called me.

27
00:01:58,850 --> 00:02:00,450
Why do you have to interfere?

28
00:02:02,410 --> 00:02:03,450
To make money.

29
00:02:04,750 --> 00:02:06,730
But more important than making money,

30
00:02:06,730 --> 00:02:08,330
I want to make you miserable.

31
00:02:12,370 --> 00:02:13,560
Young Master Lu,

32
00:02:13,770 --> 00:02:15,570
you are really boring.

33
00:02:15,970 --> 00:02:17,329
I can't compare to you.

34
00:02:21,770 --> 00:02:24,100
Recovering from an injury must be boring.

35
00:02:28,910 --> 00:02:29,710
Draw a card.

36
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:35,020
You are really no fun.

37
00:02:38,820 --> 00:02:40,420
It seems it still hurts a bit.

38
00:02:58,340 --> 00:03:00,410
[Kill Lu Ye]

39
00:03:40,490 --> 00:03:41,530
What are you doing?

40
00:03:41,530 --> 00:03:43,060
I should be asking you this.

41
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:49,040
You're allowed to kill me,

42
00:03:49,610 --> 00:03:51,050
but I can't strike first?

43
00:03:51,570 --> 00:03:52,970
Are you trying to attract

44
00:03:53,190 --> 00:03:55,590
everyone in this carriage by shooting now?

45
00:03:57,250 --> 00:03:58,170
So what?

46
00:03:58,690 --> 00:04:00,140
This is not Ningcheng.

47
00:04:00,290 --> 00:04:00,990
Right.

48
00:04:01,450 --> 00:04:03,380
So no one will collect your corpse.

49
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:07,830
There's no bullets.

50
00:04:08,490 --> 00:04:09,510
Fooled you.

51
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,660
Have you figured out how to kill me?

52
00:04:13,660 --> 00:04:15,920
If not, it's my turn.

53
00:04:40,130 --> 00:04:40,730
A gun.

54
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:53,240
This is not something we should see.

55
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:08,960
I'm sorry.

56
00:05:08,990 --> 00:05:10,230
I'm really sorry

57
00:05:10,410 --> 00:05:12,010
to have kept you two waiting.

58
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:13,000
Butler Wang,

59
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:14,080
is the cargo okay?

60
00:05:14,090 --> 00:05:15,870
No problem.

61
00:05:15,990 --> 00:05:17,390
Not a single bottle broken.

62
00:05:17,390 --> 00:05:18,310
Mr. William

63
00:05:18,430 --> 00:05:19,510
is very satisfied.

64
00:05:19,830 --> 00:05:21,630
He asked me to thank you two.

65
00:05:22,870 --> 00:05:24,000
Please accept this.

66
00:05:24,690 --> 00:05:25,820
Please accept this.

67
00:05:26,830 --> 00:05:28,750
Mr. William is so generous.

68
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:30,650
He is indeed a prominent figure
in Jiangcheng.

69
00:05:30,650 --> 00:05:31,250
Alright.

70
00:05:31,470 --> 00:05:32,670
Since the cargo is fine,

71
00:05:32,670 --> 00:05:34,270
we won't bother you anymore.

72
00:05:34,870 --> 00:05:35,870
Please wait.

73
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:38,159
It's not easy to escort the goods.

74
00:05:38,310 --> 00:05:39,510
Mr. William

75
00:05:39,510 --> 00:05:41,830
prepared two gifts for you to take back.

76
00:05:42,110 --> 00:05:43,990
They are imported Cuban cigars.

77
00:05:44,230 --> 00:05:46,560
If Mr. Shen remembers correctly,

78
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,120
these are Chief Xu's favorites.

79
00:05:49,630 --> 00:05:51,030
That's very thoughtful.

80
00:05:52,150 --> 00:05:53,830
But coincidentally,

81
00:05:53,950 --> 00:05:55,470
these cigars

82
00:05:55,490 --> 00:05:56,690
are stuck at customs.

83
00:05:56,870 --> 00:05:58,230
You'll have to wait a bit.

84
00:05:58,230 --> 00:06:01,870
Why don't you two stay a few more days?

85
00:06:04,110 --> 00:06:05,270
I have no problem with that.

86
00:06:05,270 --> 00:06:07,150
I've heard Jiangcheng
has lots of great food and fun.

87
00:06:07,150 --> 00:06:07,980
Yes.

88
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:09,460
Tianbai,

89
00:06:11,630 --> 00:06:12,490
what about you?

90
00:06:15,470 --> 00:06:16,420
Then I’ll have to trouble you.

91
00:06:16,420 --> 00:06:17,480
However...

92
00:06:17,510 --> 00:06:18,510
Not at all.

93
00:06:18,510 --> 00:06:20,310
I don't want to stay with him.

94
00:06:20,670 --> 00:06:21,590
What do you mean?

95
00:06:21,590 --> 00:06:22,390
I'm telling you,

96
00:06:22,390 --> 00:06:24,070
I'll go wherever you go today.

97
00:06:24,270 --> 00:06:25,870
What if you poison and kill me?

98
00:06:25,870 --> 00:06:26,730
Suit yourself.

99
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:30,280
Do you think I really want to follow you?

100
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:34,890
Don't look back.

101
00:06:34,909 --> 00:06:36,310
Someone is following us.

102
00:06:37,130 --> 00:06:38,070
You caught that.

103
00:06:38,860 --> 00:06:41,030
You never call me Tianbai.

104
00:06:43,050 --> 00:06:43,850
Tianbai,

105
00:06:44,090 --> 00:06:44,950
what about you?

106
00:06:45,990 --> 00:06:46,870
Pretty smart.

107
00:06:47,070 --> 00:06:47,950
On the left.

108
00:06:52,890 --> 00:06:53,590
What do you mean?

109
00:06:53,590 --> 00:06:55,120
Why are you walking so fast?

110
00:06:55,950 --> 00:06:56,670
What do you mean?

111
00:06:56,670 --> 00:06:57,800
You won't talk, huh?

112
00:06:58,210 --> 00:06:59,540
I can go wherever I want.

113
00:06:59,550 --> 00:07:00,750
I'll just follow you.

114
00:07:01,970 --> 00:07:04,130
The Duke of Zhou was named Ji Dan.

115
00:07:04,220 --> 00:07:06,300
He was the fourth son of King Wen of Zhou,

116
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:07,930
and the younger brother of King Wu.

117
00:07:07,930 --> 00:07:09,930
Because his fief was in Zhou,

118
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:11,870
he was appointed as the highest duke,

119
00:07:11,870 --> 00:07:13,530
hence called the Duke of Zhou.

120
00:07:13,630 --> 00:07:16,070
He twice aided King Wu in his campaign
to overthrow King Zhou.

121
00:07:14,110 --> 00:07:17,010
[Jiangcheng Library]

122
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:17,780
After King Wu's death,

123
00:07:17,930 --> 00:07:19,790
he acted as regent for King Cheng,

124
00:07:19,890 --> 00:07:20,830
established rites and music,

125
00:07:20,830 --> 00:07:22,740
and brought great order to the world.

126
00:07:22,740 --> 00:07:23,700
He claimed that

127
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:25,560
he would wring his hair three times
during a bath

128
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:27,830
and spit out his food three times
during a meal.

129
00:07:27,830 --> 00:07:29,470
all to rise and receive worthy men.

130
00:07:29,470 --> 00:07:31,690
I didn't expect a gentleman
to come to a place like this.

131
00:07:31,690 --> 00:07:32,920
This is a storytelling house.

132
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:34,640
Many women tell stories here.

133
00:07:34,830 --> 00:07:37,630
Dignitaries love to come here
to appear cultured.

134
00:07:38,150 --> 00:07:39,070
It's safer.

135
00:07:40,220 --> 00:07:42,990
The Industrial and Commercial Bureau here
has long been controlled by foreigners.

136
00:07:42,990 --> 00:07:45,090
They have always had conflicts
with the Chinese Chamber of Commerce.

137
00:07:45,090 --> 00:07:47,190
Recently, the foreigners plan to
revise the regulations,

138
00:07:47,190 --> 00:07:49,240
adding many new excuses to collect money.

139
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:51,120
The Chinese Chamber of Commerce
is against it

140
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:53,180
and have been protesting for a month.

141
00:07:53,310 --> 00:07:56,270
Those atms are meant to suppress them.

142
00:07:56,990 --> 00:07:58,790
But this matter can't be revealed.

143
00:07:58,790 --> 00:07:59,850
Once it is exposed,

144
00:07:59,990 --> 00:08:01,550
Jiangcheng will definitely be in chaos.

145
00:08:01,550 --> 00:08:04,220
That's why William got the goods
from Ningcheng.

146
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:07,420
And hired two completely unrelated gangs
to escort them.

147
00:08:09,110 --> 00:08:10,050
I didn't expect

148
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:12,640
that we two unlucky guys
would stumble upon his secret.

149
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:16,000
Maybe we will die in a foreign land.

150
00:08:23,150 --> 00:08:24,930
They've been sending people to follow us.

151
00:08:24,930 --> 00:08:26,160
Have they already found out?

152
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:27,160
Not necessarily.

153
00:08:27,450 --> 00:08:29,640
It might just be
the government's procedure.

154
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:31,320
These officials are very cautious.

155
00:08:31,320 --> 00:08:32,990
They usually take three to five days
to inspect the goods.

156
00:08:32,990 --> 00:08:35,919
Before that, they naturally have someone
follow us.

157
00:08:36,980 --> 00:08:39,039
William's attitude is still uncertain.

158
00:08:39,039 --> 00:08:40,330
If we run away in a hurry,

159
00:08:40,330 --> 00:08:42,260
it will only arouse his suspicion.

160
00:08:42,330 --> 00:08:43,130
That's right.

161
00:08:50,090 --> 00:08:51,690
As expected of Officer Shen,

162
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:54,310
you know these things
like the back of your hand.

163
00:08:54,310 --> 00:08:55,840
Even if you joined the gang,

164
00:08:55,870 --> 00:08:58,330
your time in the police force
wasn't in vain.

165
00:08:59,820 --> 00:09:01,680
Instead of being sarcastic here,

166
00:09:02,290 --> 00:09:04,720
you should figure out who is trying
to harm us.

167
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:06,730
What's your brilliant idea, Officer Shen?

168
00:09:06,730 --> 00:09:08,130
If you hadn't gone crazy,

169
00:09:08,360 --> 00:09:10,960
how could we have gotten into
such big trouble?

170
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:12,280
Is that so?

171
00:09:12,830 --> 00:09:16,030
Why do I remember it was because
someone wanted to kill me?

172
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:17,960
Don't you want to kill me?

173
00:09:18,740 --> 00:09:19,540
Of course I do.

174
00:09:22,740 --> 00:09:24,500
Then why don't you do it?

175
00:09:26,770 --> 00:09:27,770
Shen Tianbai.

176
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:29,280
Do you think I'm an idiot?

177
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:30,300
If I kill you,

178
00:09:30,490 --> 00:09:31,820
how will I get out alone?

179
00:09:38,950 --> 00:09:39,870
But,

180
00:09:40,890 --> 00:09:42,010
once this is over,

181
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:44,100
I will still find a chance to kill you.

182
00:09:45,910 --> 00:09:47,070
Likewise.

183
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:54,400
I've already tried to contact Uncle Zhong.

184
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:55,850
Let's wait a bit longer.

185
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:56,800
Until then,

186
00:09:57,830 --> 00:09:58,890
let's wait and see.

187
00:10:10,810 --> 00:10:11,970
There's a change of plan.

188
00:10:11,970 --> 00:10:12,970
We leave tonight.

189
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:15,230
We can't take the train.

190
00:10:15,650 --> 00:10:18,250
-We have to take the water route.
-Water route.

191
00:10:26,740 --> 00:10:29,540
But I'm a little surprised.

192
00:10:30,180 --> 00:10:32,380
I definitely can't escape alone,

193
00:10:32,860 --> 00:10:34,620
but with your skills,

194
00:10:34,710 --> 00:10:38,170
we have a 70 or 80% chance of escaping
in the middle of the night.

195
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:39,640
Why did you tell me?

196
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:43,480
Wouldn't it be perfect to let me die here?

197
00:10:50,590 --> 00:10:51,680
If I left,

198
00:10:52,030 --> 00:10:53,430
wouldn't you sell me out?

199
00:10:56,100 --> 00:10:56,970
Bingo.

200
00:10:57,570 --> 00:11:00,010
Good thing you made the right choice.

201
00:11:04,140 --> 00:11:06,300
Mr. Shen, Mr. Lu,

202
00:11:06,470 --> 00:11:09,390
Mr. William would like to
buy you two a drink tonight.
